item.p:
at a site listed in an inventory in accordance with Article 5 of the Federal Act of 1 July 1966

  SR 451
	 on the Protection of Nature and Cultural Heritage (NCHA);

fails to comply within or outside of the forest with the regulations on measures for the prevention and remediation of forest damage and measures against diseases and pests that may threaten the forest internally; Article 233 of the Criminal Code

 SR 311.0
	 is reserved;

fails to comply with the regulations on the origin, use, trade in and safeguarding of forest reproductive material. If an offence is at the same time an offence against the customs legislation, it is prosecuted and judged under the Customs Act of 1 October 1925

 [BS 6 465; AS 1956 587; 1959 1343 Art. 11 No III; 1973 644; 1974 1857 Annex No 7; 1980 1793 No I 1; 1992 1670 No III; 1994 1634 No I 3; 1995 1816; 1996 3371 Annex 2 No 2; 1997 2465 Annex No 13; 2000 1300 Art. 92, 1891 No VI 6; 2002 248 No I 1 Art. 41; 2004 4763 Annex No II 1; 2006 2197 Annex No 50. AS 2007 1411 Art. 131 para. 1]. See now: the Customs Act of 18 March 2005 (SR 631.0).
	;

the Federal Act of 11 October 1902

 [BS 9 521; AS 1954 559 No I 5, 1956 1215, 1965 321 Art. 60, 1969 500, 1971 1190, 1977 2249 No I 11.11, 1985 660No I 23, 1988 1696 Art. 7]
	 on the Supervision of the Forest Police by the Confederation;

the Federal Act of 21 March 1969

 [AS 1970 761]
	 on Investment Credits for the Forestry Sector in the Mountain Region;

the Federal Decree of 21 December 1956

 [AS 1957 317; 1977 2249No I 11.12]
	 on the Contribution of the Confederation to the Rehabilitation of Forests Infested with Chestnut Blight;
